# Client brand files never belong in a public repo. The registry ships with the
# house brand, the neutral skin, the template, and one synthetic stub; every
# other brand file is created locally against a real client's design system and
# stays on the machine that made it.
#
# The negations below are what keep the shipped four tracked. If you add a brand
# for a client, it is ignored on purpose -- do not `git add -f` it.
skills/diagram/references/brands/*.md
!skills/diagram/references/brands/_default.md
!skills/diagram/references/brands/_template.md
!skills/diagram/references/brands/_example-stub.md
!skills/diagram/references/brands/cklph.md

# The skill moved from skills/cklph-diagram/ to skills/diagram/ in 3.7.0. A
# checkout leaves git-ignored client files behind in the old folder, so it stays
# ignored until they are moved out.
skills/cklph-diagram/

# Local-only backup of client brand files taken during an upgrade. Same rule as
# above: client design systems do not belong in a public repo.
.local-brands-backup/

# Build output and packaging artifacts
out/
*.skill
*.tar.gz

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Licensed brand font files: used in deliverables, never published in this public repo.
skills/diagram/references/brands/fonts/
